  <p>
    Influenza and Respiratory Syncytial Virus (RSV) are both respiratory viruses that circulate during fall and winter
    months and share many overlapping symptoms. However, they differ in who they most severely affect, how symptoms
    progress, and what treatments are available. Knowing the differences can help you seek appropriate care —
    especially for the very young and very old.
  </p>

